        "description": "Plain CUDA allocator segments, so the copy-engine IPC all-to-all can start.",
        "notes": "Derived from `default` (the profile B300 selects). Audit 2026-10-23 (Cosmos3/Wan2.2 finding 1): the harness exports PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True (scripts/devbox_run_cases.sh); sharing an expandable segment needs pidfd_getfd, which RunPod containers deny, so every sglang SP cell of the round logged 'IPC all-to-all (multi-rank) unavailable (pidfd_getfd: Operation not permitted); using NCCL'. TRT-LLM already carries this override for the same reason. Accept the arm only if that line is absent. Promoted from cand-noexp by the 2026-10-22 4xB300 fourth-wave A/B: 25.03 s against default 25.75 s (kv-gather 25.61, auto attention 25.73). RunPod containers deny pidfd_getfd, so under the harness's expandable_segments:True sglang's multi-rank IPC all-to-all fell back to NCCL ('IPC all-to-all (multi-rank) unavailable'); sglang#45948 (merged 2026-10-23, not in this round's pin 82f7249c) fixes it in sglang. TRT-LLM runs with the same override for the same reason.",
