        "description": "Blackwell LightX2V Cosmos3 i2v: the upstream Nano omni config, torch SDPA, CFG 2 x Ulysses 2, resident.",
        "notes": "Onboarded 2026-10-23 from the audits (image finding 3, Cosmos3/Wan2.2 finding 6): LightX2V 19c19614 has RUNNER_REGISTER('cosmos3') with tasks t2i/t2v/i2v (lightx2v/models/runners/cosmos3/cosmos3_runner.py) and configs/cosmos3/cosmos3_nano_omni.json matches this case: 35 steps (the harness writes infer_steps from the case), sample_guide_scale 6.0, sample_shift 10, 720x1280, resolution and duration templates off, one-pass norms, cosmos3_rope; offload off. Attention: torch_sdpa, LightX2V's own default for Cosmos3 (transformer_weights.py) and cuDNN / flash SDPA on B300; the upstream configs name flash_attn3 (Hopper-only) or flash_attn2 (the sm80 path). Every attention call is one sequence (_infer_attn passes a single cu_seqlens segment), so torch_sdpa ignoring cu_seqlens is exact. Text is tokenized to its real length (no padding), as in the other rows. Compile: Cosmos3TransformerInfer never calls init_compile/run_block at 19c19614, so use_compile is ignored and the transformer runs eager, LightX2V's only path. The reference arrives as image_path (a data URI). Two differences from sglang, both LightX2V's own: it resizes the image straight to 1280x720 (no aspect-preserving crop: numerics only), and VAE-encodes it repeated across all 189 frames before keeping the first latent (_prepare_i2v_condition_latents), the extra ~1.9 s TRT-LLM also pays. VALIDATION PENDING (wave 4, 4xB300). First measured by the wave-4 A/B (scripts/run_b300_ab_20261022.sh, WAVE=4).",
